      }
      meta {
        last_updated {
          value_us: 1572560963356000
          timezone: "+11:00"
          precision: MILLISECOND
        }
      }
      text {
        status {
          value: GENERATED
        }
        div {
          value: "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><h2>StructureMapTargetListMode</h2><div><p>If field is a list, how to manage the production.</p>\n</div><p>This code system http://hl7.org/fhir/map-target-list-mode defines the following codes:</p><table class=\"codes\"><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\"><b>Code</b></td><td><b>Display</b></td><td><b>Definition</b></td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">first<a name=\"map-target-list-mode-first\"> </a></td><td>First</td><td>when the target list is being assembled, the items for this rule go first. If more than one rule defines a first item (for a given instance of mapping) then this is an error.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">share<a name=\"map-target-list-mode-share\"> </a></td><td>Share</td><td>the target instance is shared with the target instances generated by another rule (up to the first common n items, then create new ones).</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">last<a name=\"map-target-list-mode-last\"> </a></td><td>Last</td><td>when the target list is being assembled, the items for this rule go last. If more than one rule defines a last item (for a given instance of mapping) then this is an error.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">collate<a name=\"map-target-list-mode-collate\"> </a></td><td>Collate</td><td>re-use the first item in the list, and keep adding content to it.</td></tr></table></div>"
        }
      }
      extension {
        url {
          value: "http://hl7.org/fhir/StructureDefinition/structuredefinition-wg"
        }
        value {
          code {
            value: "fhir"
          }
        }
      }
      extension {
