        }
        div {
          value: "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><h2>ExpansionProcessingRule</h2><div><p>Defines how concepts are processed into the expansion when it\'s for UI presentation.</p>\n</div><p>This code system http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/expansion-processing-rule defines the following codes:</p><table class=\"codes\"><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\"><b>Code</b></td><td><b>Display</b></td><td><b>Definition</b></td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">all-codes<a name=\"expansion-processing-rule-all-codes\"> </a></td><td>All Codes</td><td>The expansion (when in UI mode) includes all codes *and* any defined groups (in extensions).</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">ungrouped<a name=\"expansion-processing-rule-ungrouped\"> </a></td><td>Groups + Ungrouped codes</td><td>The expanion (when in UI mode) lists the groups, and then any codes that have not been included in a group.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">groups-only<a name=\"expansion-processing-rule-groups-only\"> </a></td><td>Groups Only</td><td>The expansion (when in UI mode) only includes the defined groups.</td></tr></table></div>"
        }
      }
      url {
        value: "http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/expansion-processing-rule"
      }
      identifier {
        system {
          value: "urn:ietf:rfc:3986"
